  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="35015b27-8f20-52ff-94eb-8677926a3764" activityNameId="d19ddd34-b5bd-5964-af72-01105f149ce9" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Nitric acid, 50% in H2O, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Nitric acid, 50% in H2O, at plant
Manufacturing process starting with ammonia is considered, plus consumption of auxiliaries, energy, infrastructure and land use, as well as generation of wastes and emissions into air and water. Transport of the raw materials, auxiliaries and wastes is included, transport and storage of the final product nitric acid are not included. No byproducts or coproducts are considered. Transcient or unstable operations are not considered, but the production during stable operation conditions. Emissions to air are considered as emanating in a high population density area. Emissions into water are assumed to be emitted into rivers. Solid wastes are assumed to be sent to landfill. Average values, based on Patyk 1997 and others (see report). Inventory refers to 1 kg 100% nitric acid.;
CAS number: 007697-37-2; 
Formula: HNO3; 
Synonyms: weak nitric acid; 
UUID: 7a00c9c5-a12c-35bc-8f31-f557d19bb1d0
The inventory includes the oxidation of ammonia and the absorption steps and the final dilution of the acid.
Location: European average values
Technology: mostly average technology (Patyk 1997) used in european weak nitric acid production plants
Time period: Values based basically on literature using data from the 1990s and on reports from 2000-2001.
Production volume: na
Sampling: average values from the most confident data source for each input/output 
Extrapolations: Transports based on standard distances of Ecoinvent. Infrastructure: proxy module used (chemical plant, organics)
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_7a00c9c5-a12c-35bc-8f31-f557d19bb1d0.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
